{
  "name": "Fallen-Star Jester Musket",
  "category": "combat",
  "concept": {
    "literalSynthesis": "A two-handed jester's musket carries the bright, pointed shape and yellow glow of a fallen star in its shot.",
    "coreMechanic": "Fire one cursor-aimed ranged shot every 32 ticks, consuming a fallen star as native ammunition. The 31-damage musket shot travels in a deliberate downward gravity arc. When it hits an NPC, it creates one smaller, slower-homing star with 10 authored damage, giving a successful shot a modest follow-up without a wide burst or unbounded chain. The star is ammunition, not a projectile copied from its native AI. The weapon remains reusable; ammunition is paid through native ammo consumption.",
    "parentAContribution": "The Jester's musket supplies the two-handed ranged launcher identity, 31 base damage, 5.25 knockback, blue rarity, and its measured 32-tick shooting tempo. Its star-themed shot motivates the authored gravity-arc projectile.",
    "parentBContribution": "The Fallen Star contributes the actual fallen-star ammunition requirement and the small, bright star identity used for the on-hit follow-up. Its damage sentinel is not treated as a weapon stat.",
    "playerExperience": "Aim and fire at the normal musket cadence. Each primary shot consumes a fallen star; a hit can produce one modest homing follow-up. The follow-up is secondary damage, not guaranteed if the shot misses.",
    "plannedPlayerActions": [
      {
        "input": "primary_use",
        "intent": "Aim and fire a single gravity-arc musket shot, spending one selected fallen-star ammunition unit; a hit creates one smaller homing star."
      }
    ]
  },
